From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Modrinth Enhanced <patches@modrinth-enhanced.invalid>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:23:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Remove telemetry

Crash reporting and the survey embeds are removed, and the Modrinth
analytics endpoints the launcher itself posts to are no longer called.
Upstream already dropped PostHog product analytics:

* `helpers/error-reporting.ts` no longer loads `@sentry/vue`; errors are
  logged locally, as they are in upstream development builds.
* The third-party Tally embed is gone. It was loaded from `index.html`
  on every start for the app's own survey popup, and injected again by
  the Modrinth Hosting panel in `@modrinth/ui` when a server carries a
  survey notice. Neither loads it now, and the app no longer fetches the
  survey list, so the popup that carries the signed-in Modrinth user id
  never appears.
* `analytics/playtime` and `analytics/minecraft-server-play` are no
  longer posted from `app-lib`. The latter also removes a Mojang session
  handshake whose only purpose was to authenticate that report.
* The webview CSP no longer allows Sentry or Tally at all, so this is
  enforced rather than merely intended.

`@sentry/vue` stays in package.json. Removing it would mean carrying a
patch against the lockfile, and nothing imports it any more, so it does
not end up in a build.

Download attribution is deliberately left in place: it is a header on
downloads the user already requested and is what credits project authors
for them.
